Package: ubuntu-gts9u-device
Version: 1.3
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Ubuntu gts9uwifi port contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Depends: systemd, e2fsprogs, gdisk, parted, util-linux, cloud-guest-utils,
 protection-domain-mapper, bluez, alsa-ucm-conf,
 hexagonrpcd, libssc, iio-sensor-proxy
Description: Device support for the Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 Ultra Wi-Fi
 Board-specific integration for the SM-X910 (gts9uwifi) running an Ubuntu
 userspace on a mainline kernel:
 .
  * first-boot root filesystem expansion on the microSD;
  * ANA38407 panel recovery after Samsung's cold-boot hand-off;
  * late audio DSP boot, which the ALSA card and the sensors both depend on;
  * the native Bluetooth address, read read-only from the Samsung EFS;
  * the UCM profile for the four CS35L45 speakers and the digital microphones;
  * the sensor recovery that hands the DSP accelerometer to the desktop, and
    the accelerometer mount matrix this panel needs;
  * safe, hash-pinned STM32 firmware validation for the EF-DX920 pogo keyboard;
  * initramfs pruning for this device's 8 MiB init_boot partition.
 .
 Hardware enablement lives in the kernel and in the firmware overlay installed
 by the TWRP ZIP; this package only carries userspace integration.
